comments.body:
Follow-up from translating the prototype into an upstream-ready patch against current `main` (`8bd9c2032e242bfc018e75015e93f29607a81289`):

I found and corrected one prototype-only integration mistake before upstreaming: `POINTER_ONLY_OPS` is local to `analyze_kernel_access`, so the memoized helper must close over it directly. The durable V2 now preserves `tt.make_tensor_ptr` / `tt.advance` / `tt.make_tensor_descriptor` base-pointer-only traversal instead of treating metadata operands as pointers.

Current evidence:

- repository-local V2 suite: 8 focused tests pass;
- real analyzer probes in two independent PyTorch environments: pointer-only graph writes only `out_ptr` and remains epilogue-fusion eligible;
- depth-80 shared graph writes only `out_ptr` but correctly reports many paths and refuses fusion;
- explicit cycle fails closed;
- a current-main patch modifies only `torch/_higher_order_ops/triton_kernel_wrap.py` and `test/inductor/test_triton_kernels.py`;
- the regression uses a bounded dict lookup counter, so the old exponential traversal fails quickly rather than hanging CI;
- patched source and focused upstream-test syntax compile.

The current patch artifact SHA-256 is `4ecd43428ef262316b92aad8fd113a6aad3f877ca502037df70ab1ad99e89cdc`. I have not pushed a PR yet. This remains independent of #193227: that PR avoids repeated whole-kernel analysis, while this change bounds the first analysis itself.
